# ROLE: Re-exports requirements.lock.txt (hashed, no dev deps) from uv.lock.
# ARCH REF: D-03
# OWNS: Export invocation
# DOES NOT OWN: Resolving dependencies (uv lock)
# CONNECTS TO (external boundaries only):
#   - called by tests/scripts/test_export_requirements.py: main, ROOT
#   - called by requirements.lock.txt: regenerated by this script
#   - emits/consumes: none
# INSTRUCTIONS (strict, imperative):
#   1. Implement only this file. If this file's contract with another file must change, stop and report; do not edit the other file.
#   2. Keep every public name and signature declared below exactly as written; they are the contract other files rely on.
#   3. Use only the standard library, the pinned dependencies in pyproject.toml, and the files listed under CONNECTS TO. Ask before adding a dependency.
#   4. Open text files with encoding="utf-8" explicitly.
#   5. Use pathlib.Path for every path; obtain base directories only from src/asf/config/paths.py; never hardcode drive letters, home directories or system temp directories (use tempfile when a scratch location is needed).
#   6. Start processes only with argument lists (never shell=True, never os.system); route OS-specific behaviour (sandbox, process tree, file locks, signals, detach) through asf.platform.select.get_platform().
#   7. Behave identically on Windows and Linux (Debian-family and Arch); when a capability is missing, degrade through the safe fallback and report it, never crash.
# FORBIDDEN: shell=True; os.system; hardcoded absolute paths; container runtimes; importing project modules not listed under CONNECTS TO; printing secrets or API keys
